  ],
  "grammar": [
    { "id": "pronouns", "title": "Personal pronouns", "body": [
      "**aní** I · **atá** you (m) · **at** you (f) · **hu** he · **hi** she · **anákhnu** we · **atém** you (pl m) · **atén** you (pl f) · **hem** they (m) · **hen** they (f).",
      "Compare Arabic: ʔana, ʔanta, ʔanti, huwa, hiya, naḥnu. Same Semitic family resemblance, as with gender in 'you'."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "אֲנִי וֵנוּ, וְאַתְּ?", "tr": "aní Venu, ve-át?", "en": "I'm Venu, and you (f)?" },
      { "text": "הֵם סְטוּדֶנְטִים.", "tr": "hem studéntim.", "en": "They're students." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "pr1", "prompt": "Say: I'm Venu.", "answer": "אֲנִי וֵנוּ.", "tr": "aní Venu." },
      { "id": "pr2", "prompt": "Ask a woman: and you?", "answer": "וְאַתְּ?", "tr": "ve-át?" },
      { "id": "pr3", "prompt": "Say: She's from Tel Aviv.", "answer": "הִיא מִתֵּל אָבִיב.", "tr": "hi mi-tel avív." },
      { "id": "pr4", "prompt": "Say: We're friends.", "answer": "אֲנַחְנוּ חֲבֵרִים.", "tr": "anákhnu khaverím." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "nocopula", "title": "No 'is/are' in the present", "concept": "copula-zero", "body": [
      "Like Arabic, Hebrew has no present-tense 'to be': **aní be-séder** = I (am) OK; **hu mi-yerushaláyim** = he (is) from Jerusalem.",
      "The past (hayá 'was') comes in Unit 6."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הַבַּיִת יָפֶה.", "tr": "ha-báyit yafé.", "en": "The house is beautiful." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "nc1", "prompt": "Say: I'm OK, thanks.", "answer": "אֲנִי בְּסֵדֶר, תּוֹדָה.", "tr": "aní be-séder, todá." },
      { "id": "nc2", "prompt": "Ask a man: Where are you from?", "answer": "מֵאֵיפֹה אַתָּה?", "tr": "me-éfo atá?" },
      { "id": "nc3", "prompt": "Say: Very good.", "answer": "טוֹב מְאוֹד.", "tr": "tov me'ód." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "present4", "title": "Present tense: four forms", "body": [
      "The Hebrew present has no persons, just **gender and number**: **loméd** (m sg) · **lomédet** (f sg) · **lomdím** (m pl) · **lomdót** (f pl). The pronoun tells you who.",
      "**aní loméd** (a man speaking) / **aní lomédet** (a woman speaking). Negate with **lo**: aní lo loméd."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הוּא לוֹמֵד רְפוּאָה, וְהִיא לוֹמֶדֶת עִבְרִית.", "tr": "hu loméd refu'á, ve-hí lomédet ivrít.", "en": "He studies medicine, and she studies Hebrew." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "p41", "prompt": "Say (as a man): I'm learning Hebrew.", "answer": "אֲנִי לוֹמֵד עִבְרִית.", "tr": "aní loméd ivrít." },
      { "id": "p42", "prompt": "Ask a woman: Do you speak English?", "answer": "אַתְּ מְדַבֶּרֶת אַנְגְּלִית?", "tr": "at medabéret anglít?" },
      { "id": "p43", "prompt": "Say: They (m) study medicine.", "answer": "הֵם לוֹמְדִים רְפוּאָה.", "tr": "hem lomdím refu'á." },
      { "id": "p44", "prompt": "Say: I don't speak Hebrew.", "answer": "אֲנִי לֹא מְדַבֵּר עִבְרִית.", "tr": "aní lo medabér ivrít." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "gender", "title": "Masculine and feminine", "concept": "gender", "body": [
      "Feminine nouns and adjectives usually end in **-a** (ה-) or **-t** (-et, -it): studént → **studéntit**, yafé → **yafá**, amerika'í → **amerika'ít**.",
      "Adjectives follow the noun and agree: **ir yafá** (a beautiful city: ir is feminine even without an ending), **báyit yafé**."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הוּא אָמֶרִיקָאִי וְהִיא אָמֶרִיקָאִית.", "tr": "hu amerika'í ve-hí amerika'ít.", "en": "He's American and she's American." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "gd1", "prompt": "Say: She's a student.", "answer": "הִיא סְטוּדֶנְטִית.", "tr": "hi studéntit." },
      { "id": "gd2", "prompt": "Say: This is a beautiful city.", "answer": "זֹאת עִיר יָפָה.", "tr": "zot ir yafá." },
      { "id": "gd3", "prompt": "Say: The house is beautiful.", "answer": "הַבַּיִת יָפֶה.", "tr": "ha-báyit yafé." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "rotse", "title": "rotsé: want", "body": [
      "**rotsé / rotsá / rotsím / rotsót** + a noun: **aní rotsé kafé**. + an infinitive (le-…): **aní rotsé lishtót** = I want to drink.",
      "Polite ordering: **efshár kafé?** (Unit 11) or just **kafé, bevakashá**."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "מָה אַתְּ רוֹצָה?", "tr": "ma at rotsá?", "en": "What do you (f) want?" }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "rt1", "prompt": "Say (as a man): I want coffee, please.", "answer": "אֲנִי רוֹצֶה קָפֶה, בְּבַקָּשָׁה.", "tr": "aní rotsé kafé, bevakashá." },
      { "id": "rt2", "prompt": "Ask a man: Do you want tea?", "answer": "אַתָּה רוֹצֶה תֵּה?", "tr": "atá rotsé te?" },
      { "id": "rt3", "prompt": "Ask a woman: What do you want?", "answer": "מָה אַתְּ רוֹצָה?", "tr": "ma at rotsá?" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "yeshli", "title": "yesh li: 'I have'", "body": [
      "Hebrew has no verb 'have'. It says **yesh li** = there is to me. Negative: **en li** = I don't have.",
      "Same idea as Levantine **ʕindi** (at me), but with 'to': li, lekhá, lakh, lo, la, lánu, lakhém, lahém."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "יֵשׁ לִי שְׁאֵלָה.", "tr": "yesh li she'elá.", "en": "I have a question." },
      { "text": "אֵין לִי זְמַן.", "tr": "en li zman.", "en": "I don't have time." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "yl1", "prompt": "Say: I have a lot of work.", "answer": "יֵשׁ לִי הַרְבֵּה עֲבוֹדָה.", "tr": "yesh li harbé avodá." },
      { "id": "yl2", "prompt": "Ask: Is there bread?", "answer": "יֵשׁ לֶחֶם?", "tr": "yesh lékhem?" },
      { "id": "yl3", "prompt": "Say: There's no sugar.", "answer": "אֵין סֻכָּר.", "tr": "en sukár." },
      { "id": "yl4", "prompt": "Ask a man: Do you have water?", "answer": "יֵשׁ לְךָ מַיִם?", "tr": "yesh lekhá máyim?" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "binyan-preview", "title": "Verb patterns (binyanim): a first look", "concept": "root-pattern", "body": [
      "Every verb is a root in a pattern (**binyan**). In the present: **pa'al** CoCeC: loméd, ohév, yodé'a; **pi'el** meCaCeC: medabér; **hif'il** meCiC: mevín.",
      "Same idea as Arabic verb forms (wazn). You don't need the names yet; just notice the shapes."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "אֲנִי מֵבִין, אֲבָל לֹא מְדַבֵּר.", "tr": "aní mevín, avál lo medabér.", "en": "I understand, but I don't speak." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "bn1", "prompt": "Say: Sorry, I don't understand.", "answer": "סְלִיחָה, אֲנִי לֹא מֵבִין.", "tr": "slikhá, aní lo mevín." },
      { "id": "bn2", "prompt": "Say: I drink tea every day.", "answer": "אֲנִי שׁוֹתֶה תֵּה כָּל יוֹם.", "tr": "aní shoté te kol yom." },
      { "id": "bn3", "prompt": "Ask a man: What are you doing?", "answer": "מָה אַתָּה עוֹשֶׂה?", "tr": "ma atá osé?" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "questions", "title": "Asking questions", "body": [
      "**ma** what · **mi** who · **éfo** where · **me-éfo** from where · **le-án** to where · **ekh** how · **láma** why · **matáy** when · **káma** how much.",
      "Yes/no questions: just raise your voice: **atá ba?** = are you coming?"
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "לָמָּה אַתָּה לוֹמֵד עֲרָבִית?", "tr": "láma atá loméd aravít?", "en": "Why are you learning Arabic?" }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "qs1", "prompt": "Ask a man: When are you coming?", "answer": "מָתַי אַתָּה בָּא?", "tr": "matáy atá ba?" },
      { "id": "qs2", "prompt": "Ask: How much is it?", "answer": "כַּמָּה זֶה?", "tr": "káma ze?" },
      { "id": "qs3", "prompt": "Ask: How do you say this in Hebrew?", "answer": "אֵיךְ אוֹמְרִים אֶת זֶה בְּעִבְרִית?", "tr": "ekh omrím et ze be-ivrít?" }
    ], "verified": false }
